Fixed. The bug was the `break` statement in the loop over `TRACKING_PARAMS` — it exited after stripping the first match, leaving subsequent tracking params (like `fbclid` when `utm_source` came first) in the URL.

Removed the `break`, so every present tracking param is now deleted. Verified with the reported case: `https://example.com/path?utm_source=news&fbclid=abc&foo=bar` → `https://example.com/path?foo=bar` (both tracking params stripped, `foo` preserved).


